  "kind": "remove",
  "title": "# Settings in place: every UI thing configures itself right where it is (Brett, Nov 7) Bug seen: Pl…",
  "asked": "# Settings in place: every UI thing configures itself right where it is (Brett, Nov 7) Bug seen: Plan Studio > toolbar `view-filter-and-sort` > Chrome settings > Behaviour shows only Search box + Collapsible, plus a note: \"Tap-to-confirm on touch and this toolbar's own override live in Settings > Plugins > Toolbars.\" Brett: unacceptable. Every toolbar (and every UI element) must have and find ALL its own settings in its own settings dialog. 1. Toolbar settings dialog (Chrome settings): show EVERY setting of that toolbar in place, including tap-to-confirm (double tap) and its own override switch (per the style-override rule: plugin/asset override ON by default, never affects its app). Remove the \"lives in Settings > ...\" note. 2. Audit every settings dialog/panel for every UI element (toolbars, banners, menus, grids, widgets, plugins, chat, etc.) across console, axHub web, AmberX, Molly. Any setting shown elsewhere or redirected must ALSO be in that element's own dialog. One source of truth: both places read/write the same setting live. 3. CI check: fails if any element's settings dialog redirects (\"lives in\", \"set in Settings >\", etc.) or if an element's declared settings aren't all reachable from its own dialog. 4. UI from assets/settings assets only, no hard-coded styling. UI Review: submit the toolbar dialog with three options (--choices). 5. Tests. Add to Shipped features. Progress: append `<time> START|DONE <step>` to PROGRESS.md here at each step; don't stop between steps. Commit, don't push. Watch live: Brett can watch the screen you are changing hot-render in the console. Whenever you start work on a screen or element, run `node framework/cli/axf.mjs focus <app> [route] [css-selector] --note \"<what you are changing>\"` (apps: console-web, axhub-web, amberx-droid, walkthrough-studio, demo, framework, console, axhub-android, voicevault). Agent cap: heavy steps (pnpm/npm/vite builds, docker node:22 test runs, Playwright) share a VPS-wide lock. Run each one as `node /opt/axf/deploy/../framework/cli/agent-slots.mjs heavy -- <command>` so only a few run at once. Model switches: a downgrade (e.g. Fable → Opus) is fine. Fable upgrades need no approval right now (Brett, Nov 4 2026: \"If it needs Fable, set it to be Fable\"): a step that needs Fable (schemas, asset types, contracts, engines/kernel, cross-app protocols) is set to Fable and runs on Fable; the switch is recorded on the build. Never launch a step on a higher model than it is pinned to: raise the step first.",
